# Build context for every service is the management root (docker-compose:
# `context: .` + `dockerfile: <Service>/Dockerfile`) so the sibling Common
# project referenced by six of the seven csproj is inside the context — a
# service-only context cannot resolve ..\Common\Common.csproj during restore.
# The rules below replace the service-local .dockerignore files, which only
# applied when the context WAS the service directory. Patterns are anchored
# from this root.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/Logs/
**/*.user
**/*.suo
**/Properties/launchSettings.json
# Firebase service account key: mounted at runtime, never baked or committed.
**/firebase-credentials.json
# Host-side probe/scratch and backup files from local debugging.
**/*.backup
**/*.backup2
resp*.bin
*.err
*.bin
# dotnet publish output from host builds: stale second copy of the app.
**/publish/
# Local tooling/scripts that must not reach the image.
*.ps1
check-health.ps1
start-all-services.ps1
start-testdrive-services.ps1
test-all-flows.ps1
test-testdrive-flow.ps1
report_test.csv
users.db*
.env
.env.example
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
DealerSystem.sln
docs/
scripts/
.config/
# The test project references the services, not the reverse, so restoring or
# publishing a service never traverses into it — but it is ~hundreds of files
# of context it does not need.
DealerSystem.Tests/
# Stray scratch file a shell redirect left at the repo root.
C\357\200\272UsersGnurtDesktopevdiff_out.txt
# Never exclude Common/, the service source dirs, or VehicleService/wwwroot/.
